From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] user32/shell32: window hot keys, SC_HOTKEY, STARTF_USEHOTKEY and ShellExecuteEx masks

WM_SETHOTKEY and WM_GETHOTKEY did nothing, so the "Shortcut key" of a
shortcut (Ctrl+Alt+letter to bring a program forward) never worked, and
WM_SYSCOMMAND SC_HOTKEY, SC_NEXTWINDOW, SC_PREVWINDOW and SC_ARRANGE were
"unimplemented". ShellExecuteEx ignored SEE_MASK_INVOKEIDLIST,
SEE_MASK_HOTKEY and SEE_MASK_CONNECTNETDRV ("flags ignored"): a program's
"Properties" command (ShellExecuteEx "properties" with
SEE_MASK_INVOKEIDLIST, as many file managers and editors use) showed
nothing.

- WM_SETHOTKEY (DefWindowProc) gives a top-level window a hot key: 1 when
  set, 2 when another window has the same key, 0 for a child window, -1
  for Escape, Space or Tab; 0 removes it. WM_GETHOTKEY reads it. Pressing
  the key sends the window WM_SYSCOMMAND SC_HOTKEY (the hot key is
  registered under a private id and the message is turned into SC_HOTKEY
  where it is taken off the queue), and DefWindowProc brings it forward,
  restoring it when minimized.
- SC_NEXTWINDOW / SC_PREVWINDOW activate the next or previous visible
  top-level window (the current one goes to the back for "next", as with
  Alt+Esc); SC_ARRANGE arranges the minimized windows.
- STARTF_USEHOTKEY: CreateProcess carries the hot key in hStdInput as on
  Windows -- not taken for a handle by the server or ntdll -- and the new
  process gives it to its first captioned top-level window;
  GetStartupInfo returns it.
- ShellExecuteEx: SEE_MASK_HOTKEY passes the hot key so;
  SEE_MASK_INVOKEIDLIST with a verb the item's shortcut menu carries out
  (properties, openas, delete, cut, copy, paste, link, pin/unpin) invokes
  it through the menu -- the dialogs on a thread of their own, so
  ShellExecuteEx returns while they are open, as on Windows;
  SEE_MASK_CONNECTNETDRV connects a share to a drive letter first.
  SEE_MASK_FLAG_DDEWAIT, ASYNCOK and UNICODE ask nothing more of this
  synchronous execute, and SEE_MASK_ICON is ignored since Windows Vista;
  only SEE_MASK_HMONITOR is still not honoured.

- explorer (a fix to 1646): the taskbar's WM_COMMAND commands are taken
  whatever lparam holds, as on Windows; a command with garbage in lparam
  (user32's own test passes 0xdeadbeef) opened the Start menu modally and
  hung the sender.

Wine's tests: user32 win 61231 tests, no failures (one todo_wine removed:
TRAY_MINIMIZE_ALL now minimizes); user32 msg and input, shell32 shlexec:
the same results as before.

Gate: test/hotkeyexec-gate.sh (the shell's desktop, test/hotkeyexec-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_SC_HOTKEY (win32u/message.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_MENU_VERBS
(shell32/shlexec.c).
